<title>BELGIUM: EU urges Austria to privatise to cut debt.</title>
<headline>EU urges Austria to privatise to cut debt.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union finance ministers recommended to Austria on Monday that it privatise state-owned companies as a way of lowering its debt to growth ratio.</p>
<p>The recommendation was part of the EU's excessive deficit procedure in which countries are advised on what courses are needed for them to meet budgetary targets in the Maastricht treaty.  </p>
<p>&quot;(The EU)...urges the Austrian government to use privatisation and other appropriate measures to put the debt ratio on a sustainable declining path,&quot; the formal recommendation to Vienna said.</p>
<p>The ministers noted that Austria's debt was on an upward trend reaching about 70 percent of Gross Domestic Product in 1996.</p>
<p>The Maastrict treaty calls for debt to be falling to or below a reference of 60 percent. -- Brussels newsroom: +32 2 287-6830</p>
